WEBVTT

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.250
Policy Holder: Leon Papas

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.879
Place of Accident:
Isidoros Village, Greece

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:38.459
Cause of Death: Serious blow
and loss of blood from a fall

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.224
Beneficiary: Ox Art Company

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.115
Man in a Maze

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.284
Man in a Maze
Beautiful...

00:01:57.284 --> 00:01:58.919
Man in a Maze
This is the Jupiter
Shrine in Morocco...

00:01:58.919 --> 00:01:59.252
This is the Jupiter
Shrine in Morocco...

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.447
...built around 150 AD.

00:02:02.022 --> 00:02:06.550
However, it is said that this
civilization originated in Greece.

00:02:07.761 --> 00:02:09.763
Back in ancient Greece...

00:02:09.763 --> 00:02:12.493
...martial arts such as
wrestling had taken place.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:17.598
The warriors staked their
faith on these bouts.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.540
Furthermore, it was
considered a sacred act...

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.565
...to place bets on the
winner of these bouts.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.007
This is the origin of gambling.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.682
Gambling has now developed
into a form of recreation...

00:02:28.682 --> 00:02:30.206
...or as a business.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:36.484
A business of betting on
whether a person lives or dies.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:40.493
In other words, the
life insurance business.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.124
That's all for today.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:52.138
Oh, class will be
canceled next week.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.807
Canceled again?

00:02:53.807 --> 00:02:57.675
I bet he'll be fired soon
if he keeps this up.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:02:59.646
Faculty Office

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.079
Faculty Office
Mr. Keaton?

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.741
Have you moved again?

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.586
Your pay slip was
sent back to us again.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.986
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:24.598
Put down your new address.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.031
Of course.

00:03:33.847 --> 00:03:34.711
Here.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.542
Thank you.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.023
Oh, by the way...

00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:45.725
...there was a telephone
call for you from England.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.419
Oh?

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.758
From an insurance
company called Lloyd's.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.757
Oh, really.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:03.843
Isn't Lloyd's the world's biggest
insurance company or something?

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:04.744
Huh?

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:08.348
A name that always comes up
whenever there's a big accident.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.950
Is it that famous?

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.044
But Lloyd's isn't like your
average insurance company.

00:04:14.521 --> 00:04:16.890
It's for people who underwrite
insurance policies.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:21.528
Like a market for underwriters
who take on the insurance.

00:04:21.528 --> 00:04:25.487
The underwriters take on the
risks under their own names.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:29.936
But, why did Mr. Keaton get
a phone call from Lloyd's?

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.837
Who knows. He sure takes
a lot of time off, though.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.935
Maybe he's in the
insurance business.

00:04:36.176 --> 00:04:37.404
Yeah, right.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.414
Not again!

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.076
Mr. Keaton took home
the tape I lent him!

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:49.114
Dodecanese, Greece

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.370
Leon Papas.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.463
An old Greek mercenary.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:11.411
I had been underwriting Papas'
insurance through Lloyd's.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.613
He had returned to his
home village recently...

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:16.343
...and seemed to have
been living a quiet life.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.947
But he died last
week in an accident.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.589
Anything suspicious
about his death?

00:05:22.589 --> 00:05:26.719
Just the fact that he fell
off a cliff seems suspicious.

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:30.959
But my biggest concern
is the named beneficiary.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.965
He had a lover named Sofia.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.469
But for some reason...

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.961
...he named Ox Art Company
of Athens as the beneficiary.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:46.472
That is the president
of Ox Art Company.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.478
Ox Bayear...

00:05:49.883 --> 00:05:51.651
You know him?

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:52.982
Well, sort of.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:55.288
Then, it's simple!

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.223
Find the real cause
of Papas' death.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:06:01.561
And find out why Ox Bayear
is the beneficiary.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:04.997
Your mission here is to
get to the bottom of that.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.200
A ticket to Greece.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.098
Good luck!

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.228
Greece, huh?

00:06:11.004 --> 00:06:11.936
Pretty nice.

00:06:16.009 --> 00:06:18.978
There's nothing interesting
in Isidoros village.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:22.448
Most of the people
actually live elsewhere...

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:25.585
...and they only return in
the summer vacation season.

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:27.382
It's like a ghost town now.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:33.414
I think it's amazing that a
2000-year-old village still exists.

00:06:33.927 --> 00:06:37.658
But the whole thing could
collapse any time now.

00:06:37.931 --> 00:06:41.067
This area is well known
for its strong winds.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.902
So, there's some bad erosion.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:43.603
Oh?

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:47.307
Oh, right. There is one
person living there.

00:06:47.307 --> 00:06:49.605
A lady named Sofia.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:51.838
But she's a real strange one.

00:06:52.312 --> 00:06:54.940
She doesn't talk to anyone.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.260
Well, Sofia?

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.562
Are you ready to talk now?

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.826
I told you that I don't know!

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:15.292
I wouldn't tell you
even if I did know.

00:07:17.971 --> 00:07:20.235
Stubborn woman.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.088
Excuse me.

00:07:35.088 --> 00:07:37.147
Could you pick up that paper?

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:43.423
Thank you.

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:45.890
I'll be right down.

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:47.931
C'mon.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:02.176
It sure is windy in this village!

00:08:10.123 --> 00:08:11.147
Is anything wrong?

00:08:11.658 --> 00:08:13.250
That man.

00:08:13.726 --> 00:08:15.626
I think I've seen him before.

00:08:22.035 --> 00:08:24.003
You are Sofia, aren't you?

00:08:24.671 --> 00:08:25.405
Please.

00:08:25.405 --> 00:08:27.430
I won't cause you any trouble.

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:31.500
I'm an agent by the
name of Keaton.

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:33.746
An agent?

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.081
From the insurance company?

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:35.911
Yes.

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:42.452
Um, Sofia...?

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:57.201
I would like to hear your
version of the accident.

00:08:58.805 --> 00:09:01.296
Could you show me the
way to Mr. Papas' house?

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:17.046
The keystone is about to fall.

00:09:25.198 --> 00:09:26.532
Sofia!

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.295
Leon's house is this way.

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:35.803
It's like a maze in here!

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.978
This is a pot for making wine.

00:09:51.324 --> 00:09:56.062
I hear a lot of old Greek ships lie
at the bottom of the Aegean Sea.

00:09:56.062 --> 00:09:58.164
I can see that it is true.

00:09:58.164 --> 00:10:02.066
You can find thousands
of those under the sea.

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.937
Just all trash.

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:06.165
There's no value.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:09.667
But you go and retrieve them.

00:10:13.146 --> 00:10:14.680
That was...

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.669
...his will.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:26.392
Are you able to talk about him?

00:10:26.392 --> 00:10:27.689
About Mr. Papas?

00:10:29.328 --> 00:10:30.530
Leon...

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:33.966
...was my hero ever
since I was a child.

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:37.236
He was the strongest
man in the village.

00:10:37.236 --> 00:10:40.865
Always standing up
for truth and justice.

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:43.843
I jumped for joy when I heard that...

00:10:43.843 --> 00:10:47.609
...he was joining the
National Liberation Front.

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:50.141
But...

00:10:51.117 --> 00:10:52.641
...that was a mistake.

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:57.146
He shouldn't have gone to war.

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:02.059
What will we do?

00:11:03.262 --> 00:11:06.866
That guy's not just
passing through.

00:11:06.866 --> 00:11:10.336
I heard that Lloyd's has taken
an interest in this case.

00:11:10.336 --> 00:11:11.064
What?

00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:14.071
If that man is an
agent from Lloyd's...

00:11:15.007 --> 00:11:18.340
...we can't just let him get away.

00:11:28.921 --> 00:11:31.524
This is really a wonderful place.

00:11:31.524 --> 00:11:33.893
The time flows so slowly.

00:11:33.893 --> 00:11:35.485
It's just worn out.

00:11:35.795 --> 00:11:38.331
Time stopped 2000 years ago.

00:11:38.331 --> 00:11:41.823
Maybe that's precisely why
Mr. Papas returned here.

00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:48.908
That day...

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:51.069
...Leon was watching
the sea just like you.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:52.277
That day?

00:11:52.745 --> 00:11:55.236
The day he came
back to the village.

00:12:04.757 --> 00:12:05.849
Leon?!

00:12:09.962 --> 00:12:11.224
Leon...

00:12:12.632 --> 00:12:16.329
But the Leon who stood
there had changed.

00:12:17.036 --> 00:12:18.437
As a result of the war...

00:12:18.437 --> 00:12:20.598
...both his body and
spirit were wounded.

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:23.809
That was when he...

00:12:23.809 --> 00:12:27.745
...started to collect old pots
and statues from sunken ships.

00:12:48.134 --> 00:12:50.770
Ancient Greek urns and
a statue of Hermes.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.499
So beautiful.

00:12:53.372 --> 00:12:55.908
From these relics, I
can feel the souls...

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:58.911
...of those who commanded
great power and fortunes.

00:12:58.911 --> 00:13:00.071
Right, Sofia?

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:08.008
By collecting these old artifacts...

00:13:08.554 --> 00:13:11.580
...Mr. Papas must've been
trying to find himself.

00:13:12.525 --> 00:13:15.824
That was when they first appeared.

00:13:28.574 --> 00:13:32.345
Since that day on, any precious
item that Leon hauled up...

00:13:32.345 --> 00:13:35.047
...was simply handed
over to Ox Bayear.

00:13:35.047 --> 00:13:36.776
What?

00:13:38.284 --> 00:13:42.015
Was he blackmailing Mr.
Papas for something?

00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:47.793
Ox was a Sergeant Major in the
British Royal Air Force...

00:13:47.793 --> 00:13:50.887
...and then became a
mercenary, fighting in Africa.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.830
Something must've
happened in Africa.

00:13:54.433 --> 00:13:58.369
Leon was always
blaming himself...

00:13:58.904 --> 00:14:02.101
...believing he betrayed his friends
and caused their deaths.

00:14:03.142 --> 00:14:05.133
Caused the death of his friends?

00:14:05.211 --> 00:14:10.148
Leon trained with the Polisario
stationed in West Sahara.

00:14:15.354 --> 00:14:18.846
He was assigned to Ox's platoon.

00:14:19.759 --> 00:14:22.895
They were eventually surrounded
by Moroccan troops...

00:14:22.895 --> 00:14:25.420
...who challenged them to a
battle at the Volubilis ruins.

00:14:28.601 --> 00:14:30.436
Blow them up, Leon.

00:14:30.436 --> 00:14:33.200
Blow them away along
with the temple!

00:14:35.641 --> 00:14:37.410
Leon!

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:38.536
No!

00:14:38.811 --> 00:14:40.369
I can't do it!

00:14:46.852 --> 00:14:48.410
Damn!

00:14:59.231 --> 00:15:03.031
Seven men died in that battle.

00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:05.504
He told me later...

00:15:05.504 --> 00:15:07.768
...that the place was
too beautiful to destroy.

00:15:15.247 --> 00:15:17.850
So, using that...

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.986
...Ox blackmailed Mr. Papas and
kept on taking the treasure.

00:15:20.986 --> 00:15:25.923
But why are they still coming
even after Mr. Papas' death?

00:15:26.726 --> 00:15:30.093
There is one treasure that
Leon never handed them.

00:15:30.629 --> 00:15:32.460
That's what they're after.

00:15:32.998 --> 00:15:33.794
Treasure?

00:15:41.907 --> 00:15:42.931
It's Ox.

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:48.581
They want to get rid of us
and search for the treasure.

00:15:48.581 --> 00:15:50.048
Is there a back door?

00:15:56.989 --> 00:15:58.013
Wait!

00:15:59.992 --> 00:16:02.228
Those men had their
jackets buttoned...

00:16:02.228 --> 00:16:04.897
...and kept their left
arms away from themselves.

00:16:04.897 --> 00:16:08.060
Which mean they're carrying
heavy guns on the left.

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:14.902
Perfect.

00:16:26.552 --> 00:16:27.541
Don't lose them!

00:16:33.692 --> 00:16:34.488
This way!

00:16:42.802 --> 00:16:44.099
Damn.

00:16:48.407 --> 00:16:49.704
Where did they go?

00:16:50.109 --> 00:16:51.744
He is a professional.

00:16:51.744 --> 00:16:53.644
I've met him somewhere before.

00:17:03.789 --> 00:17:04.949
There they are!

00:17:34.753 --> 00:17:36.188
What are you planning to do?

00:17:36.188 --> 00:17:38.622
Now, you just stand back!

00:17:44.496 --> 00:17:46.123
Pull yourself together!

00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:50.163
Damn, where did they go?

00:18:09.355 --> 00:18:10.522
Now I remember!

00:18:10.522 --> 00:18:13.548
I met you at the National Park!

00:18:15.027 --> 00:18:19.225
When I took the test for the SAS.

00:18:24.703 --> 00:18:26.071
What's the matter?

00:18:26.071 --> 00:18:27.561
Is that the best you can do?

00:18:30.009 --> 00:18:33.069
You're the instructor of
the survival training.

00:18:33.612 --> 00:18:35.045
You're the master!

00:18:50.663 --> 00:18:52.631
I did teach you once...

00:18:52.631 --> 00:18:56.335
...that a primitive weapon
like a slingshot...

00:18:56.335 --> 00:19:00.101
...is more effective in
windy places than a gun.

00:19:13.752 --> 00:19:14.878
Wow!

00:19:16.555 --> 00:19:20.150
These are the coins of Ithaki
Island, thought to be lost forever.

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:23.729
These are worth a fortune!

00:19:23.729 --> 00:19:25.720
No wonder they were after it!

00:19:25.965 --> 00:19:28.734
When they heard
about these coins...

00:19:28.734 --> 00:19:30.502
...Ox threatened Leon.

00:19:30.502 --> 00:19:32.663
But Leon defied him.

00:19:33.172 --> 00:19:36.505
It was the next day that
Leon fell off the cliff.

00:19:38.978 --> 00:19:41.347
Ox threatened Mr. Papas...

00:19:41.347 --> 00:19:44.680
...and forced him to make
Ox's company the beneficiary.

00:19:45.818 --> 00:19:46.682
And...

00:19:53.625 --> 00:19:56.287
Papas died for these coins.

00:19:57.629 --> 00:19:59.965
No matter how precious
the treasure...

00:19:59.965 --> 00:20:03.128
...there is nothing that's
worth more than a man's life.

00:20:08.107 --> 00:20:11.372
Just look at the
relief on these coins.

00:20:12.711 --> 00:20:14.679
This is Ulysses.

00:20:15.114 --> 00:20:17.216
According to legend,
after the Trojan wars...

00:20:17.216 --> 00:20:19.752
...he went through
hardships for ten years...

00:20:19.752 --> 00:20:22.414
...before he reached Ithaki Island.

00:20:23.956 --> 00:20:26.584
Ithaki was in ruins
at the time...

00:20:26.992 --> 00:20:30.052
...but he was able to find peace.

00:20:30.362 --> 00:20:34.765
That's because there was a
woman he loved on the island.

00:20:40.205 --> 00:20:44.642
Mr. Papas wanted to protect these
coins even in exchange for his life.

00:20:45.277 --> 00:20:46.744
These precious coins.

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:03.253
This belongs to you.

00:21:03.629 --> 00:21:05.722
Oh, uh, but...

00:21:06.732 --> 00:21:09.724
He would have done the same.

00:21:19.645 --> 00:21:21.408
Well, I'll take one then.

00:21:28.487 --> 00:21:32.157
What did I say?
Nothing there, right?

00:21:32.157 --> 00:21:32.816
Huh?

00:21:33.592 --> 00:21:36.220
Yes, just as you said.

00:21:53.912 --> 00:22:04.623
In a dream I had,
I noticed your distant, faint voice

00:22:04.623 --> 00:22:12.798
A scene so familiar
playing out in reality

00:22:12.798 --> 00:22:16.495
In my consciousness

00:22:17.035 --> 00:22:22.875
The sky I was searching for
brings forth a gentleness

00:22:22.875 --> 00:22:29.110
Time will give me the answer

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:40.626
In the blank scene before me

00:22:40.626 --> 00:22:46.532
I walk as the wind blows

00:22:46.532 --> 00:22:53.972
I just want to touch
it with my own hands

00:22:53.972 --> 00:23:01.845
As the wind blows against me

00:23:07.619 --> 00:23:11.223
There are those who
hunt and those who are hunted.

00:23:11.223 --> 00:23:14.359
Ever since human beings
began to hunt animals...

00:23:14.359 --> 00:23:16.657
...humans have always
been the hunters.

00:23:17.563 --> 00:23:18.764
Over the ages...

00:23:18.764 --> 00:23:21.633
...after advances in hunting
methods, in the modern age...

00:23:21.633 --> 00:23:24.124
...humans now hunt other humans.

00:23:25.204 --> 00:23:26.838
Bounty Hunter.

00:23:26.838 --> 00:23:27.673
Mercenary.

00:23:27.673 --> 00:23:28.674
Little Giant

00:23:28.674 --> 00:23:30.676
Little Giant
His name is...

00:23:30.676 --> 00:23:30.976
Little Giant

00:23:30.976 --> 00:23:33.312
Little Giant
Next time... Little Giant

00:23:33.312 --> 00:23:34.438
Little Giant
